{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE ADMIN CONSOLE SHELL — destroyed and rebuilt 4 Oct 2026 from the admin handoff
  (`design_handoff_admin_console`, README §2 and `Admin Console v9.dc.html`), and moved
  to AdminConsole v2 on 20 Oct 2026 (`design_handoff_letter_email_admin`, README §10b):
  a ground rail, one white work surface, the production signal beside the bell.
  What the old layout did, rule by rule, and where each rule lives now:
  docs/handoff/inventory/_admin.md. Decisions and deviations: docs/handoff/PHASE-ADMIN.md.
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  · Grid `auto minmax(0,1fr)`, the viewport's height; ONLY the rail's nav and <main>
    scroll (§10b). The top bar is 52px; its controls never take `min-width:0`, so only
    the crumb gives way when the bar is narrow.
  · Colour is `ag_accents('console')` — the console set of Support\Accent — in a nonced
    <style> BEFORE the stylesheets. The public palette is never emitted here.
  · Everything the shell knows comes from ONE call, `console_shell()` (ConsoleShell):
    the rail for this role, where the request is, pins, the counts, the alert pill. It is
    set at template scope, never inside a block (TwigBlockScopeTest), so every block reads it.
  · No inline handlers and no inline <script> without the nonce (admin CSP). Behaviour is
    delegated in admin.js on `data-ag-do`.
  · Every control works without script: the pin toggle, unpin and the sidebar toggle are
    forms that post; the palette and the drawer are enhancements over the rail and the
    assistant's own page.
#}
{% set shell = console_shell(admin_page|default(null)) %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ page_title|default('Admin — Africa GATES') }}</title>
<meta name="csrf-token" content="{{ csrf_token }}">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}" data-nav="shell">document.documentElement.classList.add('cn-js');
/* cnPage: what a page script binds OUTSIDE its own elements, undone when the page goes.
   console-nav.js swaps pages without a reload, so a listener on the document or window, a
   timer or an open camera would otherwise outlive its page. In the head, so it exists before
   any page script runs on a full load too. ConsoleNavTest sends every such binding here. */
window.cnPage = (function () {
  var offs = [];
  document.addEventListener('cn:unload', function () {
    var o = offs; offs = [];
    o.forEach(function (f) { try { f(); } catch (e) {} });
  });
  return {
    on: function (t, type, fn, opt) {
      t.addEventListener(type, fn, opt);
      var off = function () { t.removeEventListener(type, fn, opt); };
      offs.push(off);
      return off;
    },
    every: function (fn, ms) { var id = setInterval(fn, ms); offs.push(function () { clearInterval(id); }); return id; },
    leave: function (fn) { offs.push(fn); }
  };
})();</script>
<link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/geist/Geist-Variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">{{ ag_accents('console')|raw }}</style>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/vendor/tippy.css') }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/console/tokens.css') }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/console/console.css') }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/console/assistant.css') }}">
{% block head_styles %}{% endblock %}
  {% include 'partials/csrf-fresh.twig' %}
</head>
<body class="cn" data-console{% if not shell.can_write %} data-readonly{% endif %}{% if shell.sidebar_closed %} data-side="closed"{% endif %}>

<a href="#cnMain" class="cn-skip">Skip to content</a>
{% include 'admin/partials/nav-icons.twig' %}

<div class="cn-shell" id="cnShell">

  {# ── THE RAIL (v2, README §10b) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
     The ground, not a panel: 232px at ≥1024, a 60px icon rail at 600–1023 (labels and
     group names give way to hairlines, counts to a corner dot), and on a phone the same
     tree opened as a sheet from the tab bar's More. One tree, three widths, so the phone
     can never offer a page the desktop does not. #}
  <aside class="cn-side" id="cnSide" aria-label="Console">
    <div class="cn-side__brand" title="Africa GATES · {{ shell.role_label }}">
      <span class="cn-side__mark" aria-hidden="true">AG</span>
      <span class="cn-side__who"><span class="cn-side__name">Africa GATES</span><span class="cn-side__role">{{ shell.role_label }}</span></span>
      <button type="button" class="cn-side__close" data-ag-do="side-close" aria-label="Close menu">✕</button>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="cn-side__search" data-ag-do="palette-open" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="cnPal" title="Search">
      <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-search"/></svg>
      <span class="cn-side__search-l">Search</span>
      <kbd class="cn-side__kbd" data-cn-kbd>⌘K</kbd>
    </button>

    <nav class="cn-nav" aria-label="Console pages">
      <div class="cn-nav__top">
      {% if shell.home %}
        <a class="cn-nav__i" href="{{ shell.home.href }}" title="Home"{% if shell.current == 'dashboard' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
          <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-home"/></svg>
          <span class="cn-nav__l">Home</span>
        </a>
      {% endif %}
      {% for t in shell.top %}
        <a class="cn-nav__i" href="{{ t.href }}" title="{{ t.label }}"{% if shell.current == t.page %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
          <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-{{ t.icon }}"/></svg>
          <span class="cn-nav__l">{{ t.label }}</span>
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {% if shell.pins %}
        <div class="cn-nav__group">
          <span class="cn-nav__label" id="cnPinsLabel">Pinned</span>
          <ul aria-labelledby="cnPinsLabel">
            {% for p in shell.pins %}
              <li class="cn-pin">
                <a class="cn-nav__i" href="{{ p.href }}" title="{{ p.label }}"{% if p.href == shell.here %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                  <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-list"/></svg>
                  <span class="cn-nav__l">{{ p.label }}</span>
                  {% if p.count %}<span class="cn-nav__n">{{ p.count }}</span><span class="cn-nav__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{% endif %}
                </a>
                <form method="post" action="/admin/me/pins/{{ p.id }}/unpin" data-cn-safe data-ag-do="unpin">
                  <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="back" value="{{ shell.here }}">
                  <button type="submit" class="cn-pin__x" aria-label="Unpin {{ p.label }}" title="Unpin">✕</button>
                </form>
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      {# Every group starts open (ConsoleShell::rail); a person's own choice is applied by
         admin.js. Without script every group stays open — a collapse nobody can expand is a
         missing page. #}
      {% for g in shell.groups %}
        <div class="cn-nav__group" data-group="{{ g.key }}"{% if g.open %} data-open{% endif %}{% if g.here %} data-here{% endif %}>
          <button type="button" class="cn-nav__label cn-nav__fold" data-ag-do="nav-fold" id="cnGroup{{ loop.index }}"
                  aria-expanded="{{ g.open ? 'true' : 'false' }}" aria-controls="cnGroupList{{ loop.index }}">
            <span class="cn-nav__fold-l">{{ g.label }}</span>
            {% if g.count %}<span class="cn-nav__num{% if g.urgent %} cn-nav__num--urgent{% endif %}" aria-label="{{ g.count }} waiting">{{ g.count > 999 ? '999+' : g.count }}</span>{% endif %}
            <svg class="cn-nav__chev" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </button>
          <ul id="cnGroupList{{ loop.index }}" aria-labelledby="cnGroup{{ loop.index }}">
            {% for i in g.items %}
              {# One level, by design (owner, 20 Oct 2026): only a GROUP opens and closes; a
                 page's sub-pages are on its "also here" strip and in ⌘K, never nested here.
                 A rail item stays lit while you are on one of its sub-pages. #}
              <li>
                <a class="cn-nav__i" href="{{ i.href }}" title="{{ i.label }}"{% if shell.current == i.page or shell.current_page == i.page %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                  <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-{{ i.icon }}"/></svg>
                  <span class="cn-nav__l">{{ i.label }}</span>
                  {% if i.n %}
                    <span class="cn-nav__n{% if i.urgent %} cn-nav__n--urgent{% endif %}">{{ i.n }}{% if i.urgent %}<span class="sr-only">, urgent</span>{% endif %}</span>
                    <span class="cn-nav__dot{% if i.urgent %} cn-nav__dot--urgent{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  {% endif %}
                </a>
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </nav>

    <div class="cn-side__foot">
      {% if shell.assistant %}
        <button type="button" class="cn-nav__i cn-side__ask" data-ag-do="assist-open" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="cnAssist" title="Ask (⌘J)">
          <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-spark"/></svg>
          <span class="cn-nav__l">Ask</span>
          <kbd class="cn-side__kbd" data-cn-kbd-j>⌘J</kbd>
        </button>
      {% endif %}
      <div class="cn-acct">
        <button type="button" class="cn-nav__i cn-side__me" data-ag-do="acct-toggle" aria-haspopup="menu"
                aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cnAcct" title="{{ shell.name }}">
          <span class="cn-avatar" aria-hidden="true">{{ shell.initials }}</span>
          <span class="cn-nav__l">{{ shell.name }}</span>
          <span class="sr-only">, account menu</span>
        </button>
        <div class="cn-menu cn-menu--up" id="cnAcct" role="menu" hidden>
          <div class="cn-menu__who">
            <span class="cn-menu__name">{{ shell.name }}</span>
            {% if shell.email %}<span class="cn-menu__meta">{{ shell.email }}</span>{% endif %}
            <span class="cn-menu__meta">{{ shell.role_label }} · {{ shell.role_blurb }}</span>
          </div>
          {# One account, many roles (owner, 29 Oct 2026): the rest of this person's account,
             one POST each — switching starts that role's session. Absent unless a member
             account is signed in here and holds more than itself (account_switch()). #}
          {% set acct = account_switch() %}
          {% if acct %}
            <p class="cn-menu__h">Switch to</p>
            {% for m in acct %}{% if m.kind != 'admin' and m.live %}
              <form method="post" action="/account/switch" class="cn-menu__form" data-cn-safe>
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}"><input type="hidden" name="kind" value="{{ m.kind }}">
                <button type="submit" class="cn-menu__i" role="menuitem">{{ m.label }}<span class="cn-menu__meta"> · {{ m.sub }}</span></button>
              </form>
            {% endif %}{% endfor %}
            <hr class="cn-menu__sep">
          {% endif %}
          {% if shell.handbook %}<a class="cn-menu__i" role="menuitem" href="/admin/handbook">Handbook</a>{% endif %}
          {% if shell.assistant %}<a class="cn-menu__i" role="menuitem" href="/admin/assistant">Assistant, full page</a>{% endif %}
          <button type="button" class="cn-menu__i" role="menuitem" data-ag-do="feedback-open" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="cnFeedback">Send feedback</button>
          <a class="cn-menu__i" role="menuitem" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View the site</a>
          <a class="cn-menu__i cn-menu__i--out" role="menuitem" href="/admin/logout">Sign out</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </aside>
  <div class="cn-scrim" data-ag-do="side-close" hidden></div>

  {# ── THE WORK SURFACE: one white rounded panel, 8px in from the ground ──────── #}
  <div class="cn-col">
   <div class="cn-surface">

    <header class="cn-bar">
      <form method="post" action="/admin/me/sidebar" class="cn-bar__toggle-form" data-cn-safe>
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="closed" value="{{ shell.sidebar_closed ? '0' : '1' }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="back" value="{{ shell.here }}">
        <button type="submit" class="cn-iconbtn cn-bar__toggle" data-ag-do="side-toggle" aria-controls="cnSide"
                aria-expanded="{{ shell.sidebar_closed ? 'false' : 'true' }}" aria-label="Toggle sidebar">
          <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-sidebar"/></svg>
        </button>
      </form>
      <span class="cn-bar__title">
        {% if shell.group_label %}<span class="cn-crumb__a">{{ shell.group_label }}</span><span class="cn-crumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>{% endif %}
        <span class="cn-crumb__b">{% block topbar_crumb %}{{ block('topbar_title') }}{% endblock %}</span>
      </span>

      <button type="button" class="cn-iconbtn cn-bar__phone" data-ag-do="palette-open" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="cnPal" aria-label="Search">
        <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-search"/></svg>
      </button>
      {% if shell.assistant %}
        <button type="button" class="cn-iconbtn cn-bar__phone cn-bar__ask" data-ag-do="assist-open" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="cnAssist" aria-label="Ask">
          <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-spark"/></svg>
        </button>
      {% endif %}

      {% if shell.alert_pill %}
        {# The production signal sits left of the bell: red and pulsing while an alert is
           reaching people, amber while one may, grey while any other is open, green when
           every check passes. It is a link, so it works with no script; the words carry
           the count, never the dot alone. #}
        <a class="cn-alertpill cn-alertpill--{{ shell.alert_pill.tone }}" href="{{ shell.alert_pill.href }}">
          <span class="cn-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ shell.alert_pill.label }}
        </a>
        {# Without script the bell is a <details> that still opens. #}
        <details class="cn-menuwrap cn-bell cn-bell--{{ shell.alert_pill.tone }}">
          <summary class="cn-iconbtn cn-bell__btn" aria-label="Notifications: {{ shell.alert_pill.label }}">
            <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-bell"/></svg>
            {% if shell.alert_pill.total|default(0) > 0 %}<span class="cn-bell__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{% endif %}
          </summary>
          <div class="cn-pop cn-pop--end cn-bell__pop" role="menu">
            {% if shell.alert_pill.production|default([]) %}
              <span class="cn-bell__h cn-bell__h--prod">Production</span>
              {% for a in shell.alert_pill.production %}
                <a class="cn-bell__i cn-bell__i--{{ a.impact }}" role="menuitem" href="{{ a.href }}">
                  <span class="cn-bell__imp cn-bell__imp--{{ a.impact }}">{{ a.impact == 'affects' ? 'Affects production' : 'May affect production' }}</span>
                  <span class="cn-bell__t">{{ a.title }}</span>
                  <span class="cn-bell__m">{{ a.source }}{% if a.raised %} · {{ a.raised|when }}{% endif %}</span>
                </a>
              {% endfor %}
            {% endif %}
            {% if shell.alert_pill.items|default([]) or not shell.alert_pill.production|default([]) %}<span class="cn-bell__h">Alerts</span>{% endif %}
            {% for a in shell.alert_pill.items|default([]) %}
              <a class="cn-bell__i" role="menuitem" href="{{ a.href }}">
                <span class="cn-status cn-status--{{ a.severity }}">{{ a.severity|capitalize }}</span>
                <span class="cn-bell__t">{{ a.title }}</span>
                <span class="cn-bell__m">{{ a.source }}{% if a.raised %} · {{ a.raised|when }}{% endif %}</span>
              </a>
            {% else %}
              {% if not shell.alert_pill.production|default([]) %}<span class="cn-bell__none">Nothing needs a person. The checks are all passing.</span>{% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
            <a class="cn-pop__i cn-bell__all" role="menuitem" href="{{ shell.alert_pill.href }}">View all alerts{% if shell.alert_pill.total|default(0) > 5 %} ({{ shell.alert_pill.total }}){% endif %}</a>
          </div>
        </details>
      {% endif %}

      {% if shell.create %}
        <details class="cn-menuwrap cn-new">
          <summary class="cn-newbtn" aria-haspopup="menu">
            <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-plus"/></svg><span class="cn-newbtn__l">New</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="cn-pop cn-pop--end cn-new__pop" role="menu" aria-label="Create">
            {% for g in shell.create %}
              <div class="cn-new__g">
                <span class="cn-new__h">{{ g.label }}</span>
                {% for i in g.items %}
                  <a class="cn-new__i" role="menuitem" href="{{ i.href }}"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-{{ i.icon }}"/></svg>{{ i.label }}</a>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </details>
      {% endif %}
    </header>

    {# ── THE PAGE (§2.4) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <main class="cn-main" id="cnMain" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="cn-main__in">

        {% block page_head %}
        <div class="cn-head">
          <div class="cn-head__text">
            <div class="cn-head__eyebrow">{% block topbar_eyebrow %}{% endblock %}</div>
            <h1 class="cn-h1">{% block topbar_title %}{{ shell.label|default(page_title|default('Admin')) }}{% endblock %}</h1>
            {# A page may say what it is about more exactly than the rail's one line can. #}
            {% set head_sub %}{% block topbar_sub %}{{ shell.sub }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
            {% if head_sub|trim %}<p class="cn-head__sub">{{ head_sub }}</p>{% endif %}
          </div>
          <div class="cn-head__side">
            <div class="cn-head__actions">{% block topbar_actions %}{% endblock %}</div>
            {% if not shell.can_write %}<span class="cn-chip">Read-only for {{ shell.role_label }}</span>{% endif %}
            {% if shell.here %}
              {% if shell.pinned %}
                <form method="post" action="/admin/me/pins/{{ shell.pinned.id }}/unpin" data-cn-safe data-ag-do="unpin">
                  <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="back" value="{{ shell.here }}">
                  <button type="submit" class="cn-pin-btn" aria-pressed="true" title="Unpin from the sidebar" aria-label="Unpin from the sidebar"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-star"/></svg></button>
                </form>
              {% else %}
                <form method="post" action="/admin/me/pins" data-cn-safe data-ag-do="pin">
                  <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="href" value="{{ shell.here }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="label" value="{{ shell.label|default(page_title|default('Pinned view')) }}">
                  <button type="submit" class="cn-pin-btn" aria-pressed="false" title="Pin to the sidebar" aria-label="Pin to the sidebar"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-star"/></svg></button>
                </form>
              {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        </div>
        {% endblock %}

        {% if shell.related %}
          <nav class="cn-related" aria-label="Also here">
            {% for r in shell.related %}
              <a class="cn-related__i" href="{{ r.href }}"{% if r.on %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ r.label }}</a>
            {% endfor %}
          </nav>
        {% endif %}

        {% if flash_error %}
          <div class="cn-error" role="alert">
            <span class="cn-error__t">That did not work</span>
            <span class="cn-error__m">{{ flash_error }}</span>
            <a class="cn-pillbtn cn-pillbtn--sm" href="{{ shell.here|default('/admin/dashboard') }}">Try again</a>
          </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% if flash_notice %}<div class="cn-note" role="status">{{ flash_notice }}</div>{% endif %}

        {% block content %}{% endblock %}

      </div>
    </main>
   </div>
  </div>

  {# ── THE PHONE TAB BAR (<600px): Home · Review · Money · Alerts · More ──────── #}
  <nav class="cn-tabbar" aria-label="Console">
    {% for t in shell.tabs %}
      <a class="cn-tabbar__i" href="{{ t.href }}"{% if t.on %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-{{ t.icon }}"/></svg>{{ t.label }}
        {% if t.n %}<span class="cn-tabbar__n{% if t.urgent %} cn-tabbar__n--urgent{% endif %}">{{ t.n > 99 ? '99+' : t.n }}</span>{% endif %}
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
    <button type="button" class="cn-tabbar__i" data-ag-do="side-toggle" aria-controls="cnSide" aria-expanded="false">
      <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-more"/></svg>More
    </button>
  </nav>
</div>

{# ── OVERLAYS (§7) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}

{# Toast — a black pill at the bottom centre, 5.2 s, optional Undo. A flash from the
   last request arrives as one; without script it simply stays. #}
<div class="cn-toasts" id="cnToasts" aria-live="polite">
  {% if flash_ok %}<div class="cn-toast" role="status"><span>{{ flash_ok }}</span></div>{% endif %}
</div>

{# Confirm with reason — the reason is for the audit log, and the confirm stays disabled
   at 45% until it holds a non-space character (rule 5). Filled by admin.js. #}
<dialog class="cn-confirm" id="cnConfirm" aria-labelledby="cnConfirmT" aria-describedby="cnConfirmB">
  <form method="dialog" class="cn-confirm__card">
    <span class="cn-confirm__t" id="cnConfirmT">Are you sure?</span>
    <span class="cn-confirm__b" id="cnConfirmB"></span>
    <label class="cn-confirm__reason" data-cn-reason>Reason, for the audit log
      <input type="text" name="reason" maxlength="500" autocomplete="off" placeholder="e.g. Requested by the host, ticket &#35;4821">
    </label>
    <div class="cn-confirm__acts">
      <button type="button" class="cn-btn" value="cancel" data-cn-cancel>Cancel</button>
      <button type="submit" class="cn-btn cn-btn--primary" value="ok" data-cn-ok disabled>Confirm</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</dialog>

{# Feedback for the people who build the console. A real form, so it posts with no
   script; admin.js opens it as a dialog from the top bar. #}
<dialog class="cn-confirm" id="cnFeedback" aria-labelledby="cnFeedbackT">
  <form method="post" action="/admin/me/feedback" class="cn-confirm__card">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="page" value="{{ shell.here|default('') }}">
    <span class="cn-confirm__t" id="cnFeedbackT">Send feedback</span>
    <span class="cn-confirm__b">What is slow, confusing or missing on this page? It reaches the team with the page you are on.</span>
    <label class="cn-confirm__reason">Your feedback
      <textarea name="message" rows="4" maxlength="2000" required placeholder="e.g. I can't find where to change the vote price"></textarea>
    </label>
    <div class="cn-confirm__acts">
      <button type="button" class="cn-btn" data-ag-do="feedback-close">Cancel</button>
      <button type="submit" class="cn-btn cn-btn--primary">Send</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</dialog>
{# The assistant drawer — console-assistant.js, the same component as the expanded page
   (/admin/assistant), on the same conversation: the thread the person last spoke in, kept on
   the server. It sends the page under it as context, so "why is this one stuck?" means this
   one. Expand opens the conversation full size, with its evidence beside it. #}
{% set as_suggest = ['What should I do first this morning?', 'Why are payments stuck?', 'Which results are ready to release?', 'Anything suspicious in the nomination queue?'] %}
{% if shell.assistant %}
<div class="cn-drawer-scrim" data-ag-do="assist-close" hidden></div>
<aside class="cn-drawer as-drawer" id="cnAssist" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="cnAssistT" hidden
       data-as="drawer" data-as-suggest="{{ as_suggest|json_encode }}"
       data-as-dest="{{ shell.destinations|map(d => {label: d.label, href: d.href, group: d.group})|json_encode }}">
  <div class="cn-drawer__head">
    <div class="cn-drawer__ht">
      <span class="cn-drawer__t" id="cnAssistT" data-as-title>Assistant</span>
      <span class="cn-drawer__s">Reads this console as {{ shell.role_label }}, and the page you are on</span>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="as-iconbtn" data-as-new aria-label="New chat" title="New chat"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-plus"/></svg></button>
    <a class="as-iconbtn" href="/admin/assistant" data-as-expand aria-label="Expand" title="Expand"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-expand"/></svg></a>
    <button type="button" class="as-iconbtn" data-ag-do="assist-close" aria-label="Close" title="Close"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#ic-x"/></svg></button>
  </div>
  <div class="as-log as-log--drawer" data-as-log role="log" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Conversation"></div>
  <div class="as-compose as-compose--drawer">
    {% include 'admin/partials/assistant-composer.twig' with {as_disabled: false, as_id: 'D'} %}
  </div>
</aside>
{% endif %}

{# The command palette (§7) — ⌘K / Ctrl+K. Generated from the same tree as the rail
   (AdminNav::destinations), so a page this role cannot open is never listed. #}
<dialog class="cn-pal" id="cnPal" aria-label="Search the console">
  <form method="dialog" class="cn-pal__card">
    <input class="cn-pal__in" id="cnPalIn" type="search" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
           placeholder="Search {{ shell.destinations|length }} pages and commands" aria-label="Search the console"
           aria-controls="cnPalList" aria-autocomplete="list">
    <ul class="cn-pal__list" id="cnPalList" role="listbox" aria-label="Results">
      {% for r in shell.recent %}
        <li role="option" aria-selected="false" data-recent><a class="cn-pal__i" href="{{ r.href }}" data-cmd="{{ r.label|lower }}">{{ r.label }}<span class="cn-pal__k">Recent</span></a></li>
      {% endfor %}
      {% for d in shell.destinations %}
        <li role="option" aria-selected="false"><a class="cn-pal__i" href="{{ d.href }}" data-cmd="{{ (d.label ~ ' ' ~ d.group)|lower }}">{{ d.label }}<span class="cn-pal__k">{{ d.group }}</span></a></li>
      {% endfor %}
      {% for f in [
          ['Show nominations waiting longest', '/admin/nominations/review?sort=recv&dir=asc', 'late old overdue waiting oldest 4h'],
          ['Show paid orders with no votes', '/admin/payments', 'refund owed no votes paid stuck'],
          ['Show high alerts', '/admin/alerts?tab=high', 'alert high urgent broken down'],
        ] %}
        {% if f[1] in shell.destinations|map(d => d.href) or (f[1]|split('?')|first) in shell.destinations|map(d => d.href) %}
          <li role="option" aria-selected="false" data-filter hidden><a class="cn-pal__i" href="{{ f[1] }}" data-cmd="{{ f[2] }}">{{ f[0] }}<span class="cn-pal__k">Filter</span></a></li>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if shell.assistant %}
        <li role="option" aria-selected="false" data-ask hidden><a class="cn-pal__i" href="/admin/assistant" data-ag-do="palette-ask"><span data-ask-label>Ask the assistant</span><span class="cn-pal__k">AI</span></a></li>
        <li role="option" aria-selected="false" data-first><a class="cn-pal__i" href="/admin/assistant" data-ag-do="assist-ask" data-q="What should I do first this morning?">What should I do first?<span class="cn-pal__k">AI</span></a></li>
      {% endif %}
    </ul>
    <p class="cn-pal__none" id="cnPalNone" hidden>Nothing matches. Pages your role can't open aren't listed.</p>
    <div class="cn-pal__foot"><span>↑↓ move</span><span>↵ open</span><span>esc close</span></div>
  </form>
</dialog>

{# Script order is load-bearing: console-assistant before admin.js (which opens the drawer
   through window.cnAssist); Popper before Tippy; admin.js last. #}
<script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/console-assistant.js') }}" data-nav="shell"></script>
<script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/vendor/alpine-3.13.5.min.js') }}" data-nav="shell"></script>
<script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/vendor/popper-2.11.8.min.js') }}" data-nav="shell"></script>
<script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/vendor/tippy-6.3.7.umd.min.js') }}" data-nav="shell"></script>
{# A page's own scripts. Unmarked, the page loads the ordinary way; `data-nav="rerun"` lets
   console-nav.js swap it in, and ConsoleNavTest decides who may say that. #}
{% block foot_scripts %}{% endblock %}
<script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/admin.js') }}" data-nav="shell"></script>
<script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/console-ux.js') }}" data-nav="shell"></script>
{# Last: it listens after everything else has had its chance to handle a click. #}
<script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/console-nav.js') }}" data-nav="shell"></script>
{% include 'admin/partials/richtext.twig' %}
{% include 'admin/partials/ui.twig' %}
</body>
</html>
